course: dictionary
lesson: 1420
title: One animal, two names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same animal can have different names in different places. «Reindeer, called caribou in North America» tells you these are two names for one animal. The dictionary says a caribou is a large deer with big branching antlers, and in Europe and Asia it is called a reindeer.
explain: Use context clues to find where caribou live. Look for words like «tundra» and «migrate». The sentence about the tundra tells you that caribou live in cold northern places, where mosquitoes swarm in summer.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Caribou, called reindeer in Europe, make some of the longest land migrations of any animal.» Put in "a large deer with antlers" and it still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A caribou is a large deer of North America's Arctic and northern forests.
fact: In Europe and Asia, the same animal is called a reindeer.
fact: Both male and female caribou grow antlers, which is unusual for deer.
fact: Caribou make some of the longest land migrations of any animal.
fact: «Caribou» is a noun, and it can be singular or plural: one caribou, many caribou.
exercise: What is a caribou? | A type of snow boot | A fish that lives in the sea | A small bird that sings | *A large deer with big branching antlers
exercise: «Reindeer, called caribou in North America, have broad hooves for snow and ice.» What is the animal called in Europe? | Mosquito | *Reindeer | Tundra | Snow
exercise: «In summer the tundra has huge swarms of mosquitoes, so thick that caribou run to windy hills or snow patches to escape them.» Why do caribou run to windy hills? | To find the sea | To look for their friends | *To escape the mosquitoes | To sleep under the trees
test: Which is true about caribou antlers? | Neither males nor females grow them | Only females grow them | Only males grow them | *Both males and females grow them
test: What kind of word is caribou in «a caribou»? | Adjective | Adverb | Verb | *Noun
exam: Read: «Reindeer, called caribou in North America, have broad hooves for snow and ice.» Which word means the same animal as reindeer here? | Snow | Ice | *Caribou | Hooves
